From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wire: one shared name normalization, so demo and real
 fingerprints match

Matching kept its own normalizer, which dropped non-Latin letters and
kept a leading "the", and demo track keys used "name | artist" while
real ones use "name|artist". So demo students could miss every shared
track with real students. Both now use convex/lib/normalize.ts, and a
cross-stream test pins demo fingerprints to the onboarding builder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
